`aplan critical-path` prints the longest `effort_days`-weighted chain of dependent
tasks. Here `A -> B -> C` totals 6 days, beating the standalone `D` (5 days).

```
$ aplan critical-path
critical path: 6.0 days across 3 task(s)
  A           1.0d  Alpha
  B           3.0d  Beta
  C           2.0d  Gamma

```

```
$ aplan critical-path --format json
{
  "schema": "aplan/critical-path/v1",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "effort_days": 1.0,
      "id": "A",
      "status": "todo",
      "title": "Alpha"
    },
    {
      "effort_days": 3.0,
      "id": "B",
      "status": "todo",
      "title": "Beta"
    },
    {
      "effort_days": 2.0,
      "id": "C",
      "status": "todo",
      "title": "Gamma"
    }
  ],
  "total_effort_days": 6.0
}

```

The diagnostic formats do not apply to a rollup; they are rejected, not collapsed:

```
$ aplan critical-path --format agent
? 2
aplan: `aplan critical-path` renders a report, so it takes --format `human` or `json`, not `agent`; `agent` renders a set of findings, which `check` and `verify` do

```
